WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
MINHAZ KAZI: Welcome
to DataVis DevTalk.

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.890
I'm your host Minhaz
Kazi, developer advocate

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.540
for Data Studio.

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:09.540
In this video, we'll discuss
how you can share and publish

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:10.770
your connector.

00:00:10.770 --> 00:00:12.041
Let's get started.

00:00:12.041 --> 00:00:14.807
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.130
Let's say you have just
developed your first community

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.390
connector.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.920
You're conscious
about your health

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.970
and track your daily activities.

00:00:23.970 --> 00:00:26.690
So you've created a Google Fit
connector to track your Google

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.860
Fit data in Data Studio.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.890
You have tested
the functionality,

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:34.340
added helpful error messages,
and created separate testing

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.080
and production deployments.

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:38.660
So the connector is good
to go, but at this point,

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:41.210
the connector can be
used only on your account

00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:44.520
since you have not
shared it with others.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:47.840
When a user uses a community
connector under the hood,

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.940
Data Studio is
executing functions

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:53.330
from the connector's script
on the user's behalf.

00:00:53.330 --> 00:00:55.340
Therefore, the
user's account must

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.240
have read access to the script.

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.590
Otherwise, Data Studio
cannot execute the script.

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:03.260
If you're working a team
to develop the connector

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.080
or want a few trusted users
to try out the connector,

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.480
you must provide read access
to your connector strip

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:10.460
to these users.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:13.190
But what if you want to share
the connector with everyone?

00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:15.840
You found your Google Fit
connector to be very helpful,

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.380
and you think others can
also benefit from it.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:21.140
For that, the first step would
be to share your apps script

00:01:21.140 --> 00:01:22.820
project by link.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.090
Head over to that script
environment, open your project,

00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:27.800
hit the Share button
on the top right,

00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.750
and click on Get Sharable Link.

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.380
Make sure that the option
anyone with the link can view

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:35.250
is visible.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:37.190
If you're in a G
Suite organization,

00:01:37.190 --> 00:01:38.960
this option might
not be available

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.600
based on your
administrative settings.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.090
In this specific case, you can
either talk to your G Suite

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.210
admin to enable this
option or copy your script

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:50.120
to a non-restricted account
like a Gmail account.

00:01:50.120 --> 00:01:53.510
At this point, all users have
read access to your script.

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:56.940
Keep in mind that unless a user
has the exact link to your app

00:01:56.940 --> 00:01:59.780
script project, they will not
be able to view the code in app

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:01.462
script environment.

00:02:01.462 --> 00:02:03.295
Now to share the connector
with other users,

00:02:03.295 --> 00:02:06.817
you will also need to get
the correct deployment link.

00:02:06.817 --> 00:02:08.900
Open your connector in the
app script environment,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.690
click on Publish from the
Menu, and select Deploy

00:02:11.690 --> 00:02:13.520
from Manifest.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.050
This will show you a list of all
deployments for your connector.

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:18.890
We will cover versioning
and deployments

00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.360
in a separate video.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.690
From this interface, copy the
appropriate deployment link

00:02:23.690 --> 00:02:25.400
and share it with others.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:27.620
You can share the link
through email, social media,

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:28.970
or your own blog.

00:02:28.970 --> 00:02:30.800
Anyone who goes to
this deployment link

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.930
will be able to
use your connector,

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:36.290
configure it, connect to
their own Google Fit data,

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.570
and create their own
separate dashboards.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.320
That's pretty neat.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:42.770
You can get greater
visibility for your connector

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:45.900
by publishing it to the Data
Studio connector gallery.

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:49.514
If the connector gets
published, all Data Studio users

00:02:49.514 --> 00:02:50.930
will be able to
view the connector

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:54.380
while exploring or searching
through the gallery.

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:56.880
You can publish your
connector in two ways,

00:02:56.880 --> 00:03:00.500
either as a partner connector
or as an open source connector.

00:03:00.500 --> 00:03:02.300
If you publish as a
partner connector,

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.180
you'll need to support, deploy,
and maintain the connector

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:06.650
yourself.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:08.690
You can follow the partner
connector guidelines

00:03:08.690 --> 00:03:11.840
and submit a review
request to get started.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.030
If the connector
passes the review,

00:03:14.030 --> 00:03:17.390
it'll be included in the
gallery as a partner connector.

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:20.360
Publishing in this way helps
you and your organization

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:23.420
to get more exposure,
add your own branding,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.880
and also monetize
your connector.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.070
On the other hand, you can
publish as an open source

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.480
connector.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.260
In that case, the connector
is deployed by the Data Studio

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:35.900
DevRel team and supported
by the community.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:38.360
You can start the process
by submitting a pull request

00:03:38.360 --> 00:03:39.280
to a repository.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.994
Link is in the description.

00:03:40.994 --> 00:03:42.410
Once the pull
request is approved,

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:44.780
your connector will be
showcased in the gallery

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:46.740
as an open source connector.

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.940
This is a great way for
you to showcase your code.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.090
Publishing your connector
helps to get better visibility,

00:03:53.090 --> 00:03:55.460
reach a bigger audience,
and provide better value

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:57.330
to your existing users.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:59.210
You also become eligible
to be considered

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:01.250
for promotional activities.

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.410
So we recommend that if
you build a connector,

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:05.541
you should publish it.

00:04:05.541 --> 00:04:07.040
However, keep in
mind that you don't

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.190
have to publish to share
your connector with others.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.620
You can share by link
even without publishing

00:04:12.620 --> 00:04:15.530
and then just give the
deployment to your LT users.

00:04:15.530 --> 00:04:17.540
Hopefully you find this
sharing and publishing

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:19.790
overview for community
connectors useful.

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:21.529
You can always go to
our developer site

00:04:21.529 --> 00:04:25.010
at
developers.google.com/DataStudio

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.330
for more information.

00:04:26.330 --> 00:04:29.120
If you like this video, stay
tuned on the GCP channel

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:30.930
for more Data Studio content.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.090
Thanks for watching.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:34.840
[MUSIC PLAYING]

